1.23.1: the wipe lines up in every format

The wipe laid the comparison image in the render's box, which only
lines up for cameras that neither crop nor frame: a Polaroid's print is
the picture inside a border, a Super 8 gate is a band of the input, the
126 square a column of it. The engine now reports where the picture
landed - pj_render_geometry(): the crop taken from the input and where
it sits in the output - and writes it as a comment line after the
recipe in every JPEG ("# geometry in=W,H crop=X,Y,W,H place=X,Y
out=W,H"; recipe readers skip comment lines, and the page strips it
from the recipe box). The page lays the comparison image at the
input's pixel scale so its crop rectangle coincides with the render's
picture area, clipped to that area and to the divider; against A, A's
picture area is mapped onto the current's the same way, so two
cameras with different formats compare on the picture, not the box.
The crop and frame code in the pipeline now runs off the same geometry
struct, and renders are pixel-identical to 1.20.0 across every format
(checked), so the geometry it reports is the geometry it renders.

Also: the viewport's image rule capped overlays at the view's size,
which squashed the comparison image wherever it had to extend past the
render (gate and square crops); overlays are exempt now.

Tests: core checks the reported geometry against the rendered size
for six cameras in both crop modes; the wasm test checks the comment
line; the Chromium test checks the overlay is laid taller than the
view on super8 and clipped to the gate, and that no geometry line
reaches the recipe box.

